ers I think that  that's the part that we will have to  focus on many pro-democracy supporters  hope their success in the districts will  also carry through into elections for  Legislative Council members due in  September but the challenge isn't the  same Legislative Council elections are  held on multi seed constituency single  boat system so this means that a  pro-democracy movement will have to  minimize the number of candidates so as  not to allow bowls to be too divided  although a landslide victory isn't  expected it's possible the Legislative  Council may see more pro-democracy  candidates and if that happens Hong  Kong's pro-democracy movement will be  expanding its fight from the streets  into the corridors of power  Florence lui al jazeera Hong Kong
 

